  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Casale di Gregna</p>\r\n<p>The Roman villa at\u00a0Casale di Gregna is located at the second kilometer of the Via Anagnina (modern). The villa's first phase (second century A.D.) included a cistern built in\u00a0<em>opus mixtum</em>. The second phase (second to third centuries) also included a cistern, this time in brickwork. Also pertaining to the second phase are rooms built in\u00a0<em>opus listatum\u00a0</em>and\u00a0<em>latericium</em>, as well as a paved courtyard.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A villa at the seventh mile of the Via Latina.",
